## Visualisation — ECharts Only

- STRICTLY USE ECHARTS FOR ALL DATA VISUALISATION FOR MODULARITY.
- USE the native `echarts` npm package ONLY. No wrapper libraries. No `echarts-for-react`. No `react-echarts`. No third-party React bindings of any kind. Ever. Raw `echarts` imported directly, instance managed via refs.
- Charts must be super snappy, optimised, clean. Zero unnecessary rerenders, zero side effects, zero full redraws when data changes.
- When filters are applied or new data arrives (live charts, polling, websockets) — only the specific visual elements update. The line in a line chart. The bars in a bar chart. The slice in a pie. Not the entire chart instance. USE `setOption` with `notMerge: false` and targeted series updates. NEVER dispose and recreate.
- Chart components must isolate the ECharts instance behind a ref. No ECharts logic leaking into parent components. Parent passes data via props, chart component handles all instance lifecycle internally.
- Resize handling must be debounced and use `ResizeObserver`, not window resize events.

### ECharts Component Pattern — Follow This Exactly

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT pattern — every chart component follows this structure
const chartRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
const instanceRef = useRef<echarts.ECharts | null>(null);

// Init once on mount
useEffect(() => {
  if (chartRef.current) {
    instanceRef.current = echarts.init(chartRef.current);
  }
  return () => {
    instanceRef.current?.dispose();
  };
}, []);

// Update on data change — targeted setOption, never dispose+recreate
useEffect(() => {
  instanceRef.current?.setOption(
    { series: [{ data: newData }] },
    { notMerge: false },
  );
}, [newData]);

// Resize via ResizeObserver, debounced
useEffect(() => {
  const ro = new ResizeObserver(
    debounce(() => instanceRef.current?.resize(), 200),
  );
  if (chartRef.current) ro.observe(chartRef.current);
  return () => ro.disconnect();
}, []);
```

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG — never do this
useEffect(() => {
  instanceRef.current?.dispose(); // NO — never dispose on data change
  instanceRef.current = echarts.init(chartRef.current); // NO — never recreate on data change
  instanceRef.current.setOption(fullOptions); // NO — never pass full options on update
}, [data]);
```
